# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks every file out
# as CRLF while the repository stores LF. Pinning eol here overrides that
# regardless of any individual machine's global Git config.
#
# It matters more for this repo than for most, because the README tells readers
# to copy starter-CLAUDE.md and templates/*.md out into their own repositories
# — several of which will enforce LF. A scaffold that arrives with the wrong
# line endings makes its first commit a whole-file diff.
#
# text=auto keeps Git's binary detection: binary files are left alone.
#
# Note that the obvious guard for this ("no tracked file contains CRLF") passes
# vacuously on a Linux runner whether or not this file exists. See §2.2 of
# AI-DEV-BEST-PRACTICES.md — a property that is only observable on some
# platforms needs the mechanism asserted too.
* text=auto eol=lf
